Spec: Protected Linux authority host

Purpose:
  Open an explicitly provisioned server identity and independent durable authority stores without fixture credentials.

Owns:
  ./host.go
  ./host_test.go
  ./private_linux.go
  ./private_other.go
  ./README.md

Must:
  Accept only bounded exact schema1 configuration, absolute paths and distinct numeric IPv4 control/backend ports.
  Require caller-owned private directories, regular single-link private files and no symbolic path components; reject unsupported host platforms before opening state.
  Keep the witness outside both authority and identity backup trees; normal open requires existing files and never bootstraps or repairs missing state.
  Explicit initialization creates both databases exclusively and bootstraps only the verified owner certificate under the same root, without importing an owner private key.
  Load the server private key only from its protected identity directory, validate its standard device profile and bind durable authority to server/root identity.
  Detect changed protected directory/file identity during runtime checks and fail closed; partial initialization remains an explicit recovery condition rather than being silently overwritten.
  Keep storage and identity errors fixed without reflecting filesystem paths or key material.

Scenario: missing witness
  Given initialized authority with a removed witness
  When normal open is requested
  Then opening fails without creating a replacement witness

Scenario: conflicting initialization
  Given either state file already exists
  When initialization is requested
  Then existing state is not overwritten
